{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq projection linq projection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md","fileName":"LINQ Projection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Projection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[LINQ Query Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq projection linq projection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md","fileName":"LINQ Projection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Projection","heading":"LINQ Projection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Projection transforms each input element into a chosen output shape with `Select`. The result may be a single property, a calculated value, an anonymous object, a tuple, or a purpose-built data-transfer type.\n\nSelecting only needed fields separates the consumer's view from the source entity and can reduce data transfer for provider-backed queries. Projection also marks a conceptual boundary: filtering decides which items remain, while projection decides what each remaining item becomes.","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq projection linq projection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Projection.m